# Trivy ignore file — repo root (applies to all image scans via trivyignores: .trivyignore)
#
# Format: <CVE-ID> [expiry-date] [# comment]
# Only add entries here when:
#   a) the finding is a confirmed false positive, OR
#   b) no fix is available upstream AND a compensating control exists
# Each entry must have a comment stating the reason and a review date.
#
# ── Node.js stdlib CVEs with no Alpine-level fix at scan time ──────────────
# CVE-2026-56846: Node.js 24 HTTP/2 maxSessionMemory bypass — fixed in Node 24.21+
# Review when node:24-alpine next rebuild ships Node >= 24.21.
# CVE-2026-56846 exp:2027-01-01
